00:08:26.700 --> 00:08:32.580
fund a giant newsroom. I don't think anybody has&nbsp;
been able to do that yet, and maybe we're on our&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:32.580 --> 00:08:38.460
way to that. Who knows? But no one has as real&nbsp;
as to my mind has really been able to do exactly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:38.460 --> 00:08:45.540
that. So one level down from that is, okay, how&nbsp;
can I put together some major donors, foundations,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:45.540 --> 00:08:52.920
not nonprofit foundations, a subscription base,&nbsp;
so that so that the publication doesn't have to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:52.920 --> 00:09:00.060
singularly answer to any one of those entities&nbsp;
that's about as independent, I think. I mean,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:00.060 --> 00:09:06.540
that's pretty good. And again, I'm not I'm not&nbsp;
a purist on this. What I want to see I mean,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:06.540 --> 00:09:10.800
right now we live in a world, of course, that's&nbsp;
so far from pure. We live in a world where where&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:10.800 --> 00:09:17.580
media is is dominated by huge corporate entities&nbsp;
with either, you know, singular billionaires at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:17.580 --> 00:09:23.100
the top of them, Bloomberg News and the like,&nbsp;
or massive corporations that are that are making&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:23.100 --> 00:09:28.260
the decisions. Those are those aren't really&nbsp;
diversified at all. It's very clear who they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:28.260 --> 00:09:33.480
answer to. In fact, some of these publications&nbsp;
put right underneath the top of their articles&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:33.480 --> 00:09:38.700
presented by Chevron right now, there's, you know,&nbsp;
I guess in some ways, kudos to them for at least&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:38.700 --> 00:09:46.800
being transparent about that. But they're also&nbsp;
being explicit about who they actually serve. And&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:46.800 --> 00:09:55.800
I think ultimately you can see the independence of&nbsp;
media by the content that the media is producing.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:55.800 --> 00:10:02.220
I go back to what we produce. I, I don't think.&nbsp;
Anybody could could read what we do and say, oh,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:02.220 --> 00:10:09.060
we go easy on this or that entity or this or that&nbsp;
faction of four for this or that reason. I mean,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:09.060 --> 00:10:13.140
we are trying to follow the money no matter&nbsp;
where it goes. And we have been critical of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:13.140 --> 00:10:17.340
the Progressive Caucus at times. We have obviously&nbsp;
been critical of the Republicans. At times we've&nbsp;&nbsp;

