00:16:36.780 --> 00:16:42.420
an audience that understands those those nuances.
Speaker 3: Absolutely. And I think I think that's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:42.420 --> 00:16:47.280
actually part of I mean, there's kind of like what&nbsp;
we're doing on a day to day basis, reporting a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:47.280 --> 00:16:52.020
story on Silicon Valley Bank, reporting a story on&nbsp;
the decisions in the lead up to the East Palestine&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:52.020 --> 00:16:57.720
disaster. But I think over the long haul, what&nbsp;
we're also doing, what independent media is doing,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:58.440 --> 00:17:04.980
is saying that media needs to go back,&nbsp;
not that everything was better before,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:04.980 --> 00:17:12.180
but there needs to be a reconnection with the&nbsp;
idea that media's job is to hold accountable those&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:12.960 --> 00:17:19.920
of all parties without regard to party,&nbsp;
without regard to kind of tribal politics.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:19.920 --> 00:17:25.080
We're going to hold people accountable to&nbsp;
the facts as we know them now. And if the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:25.080 --> 00:17:30.409
facts change in the future or there's new facts&nbsp;
that arise, we're going to report on those, too.&nbsp;

00:17:30.409 --> 00:17:34.320
Speaker 1: We've been speaking with David&nbsp;
Sirota, who's founder and editor of The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:34.320 --> 00:17:38.869
Lever. You can find more at Lever Newscom.&nbsp;
Always appreciate your time and insights.&nbsp;

00:17:38.869 --> 00:17:40.560
Speaker 3: Thank you. Thanks&nbsp;
so much for having me.

